  "contract": "DMA revocation: after an unmap returns and its frames are freed, the device can no longer reach those frames (VT-d requires IOTLB invalidation after removing a translation).",
  "observed": "Asterinas never invalidates the IOTLB on DMA teardown, so a device wrote 64 bytes into a frame already recycled to an unrelated kernel allocation (QEMU vIOMMU, edu device).",
